0001> is fully faithful. We will show <MATH_0002>\nis an isomorphism. Let <MATH_0003> be any morphism.\nBy adjointness this corresponds to a morphism <MATH_0004>. By fully\nfaithfulness of <MATH_0005> this corresponds to a unique morphism <MATH_0006>.\nThus we see that post-composing by <MATH_0007> defines a bijection\n<MATH_0008>. Hence <MATH_0009> is an isomorphism.\nIf there exists an isomorphism <MATH_0010> of functors,\nthen <MATH_0011> is fully faithful. By\nLemma <REF_0001> we see\nthat <MATH_0012> is fully faithful. By the above this implies <MATH_0013>\nis an isomorphism. Thus all <MATH_0014> conditions are equivalent (and these\nconditions are also equivalent to <MATH_0015> being fully faithful).\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nPart (2) is dual to part (1).\n<STRUCT_0004>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e61ba71a06e2e90dc86a92fb513daf55d7cffa21e5c19493d91c9b58f903d05d", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:07RB:proof/0001"}, "state": "READY"}, "inventory:categories:0FWV:proof/0001": {"context_hash": "sha256:061e43e2104421c823ffb12b36fe6b2400dda11be079ccb8aa18331afd45168d", "inventory_id": "inventory:categories:0FWV:proof/0001", "kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 121452, "byte_start": 120742, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:d1788590df13e7105215b906a52a008a9b322bf527a9a97d0ec0a957d1cc2cd0", "line_end": 3437, "line_start": 3419}, "owner_tag": "0FWV", "parent_tag": "0036", "semantic_path": "proof/0001", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0036", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$u \\circ v$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$Y$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{D}$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\Mor(X,Y) \\to \\Mor(v(X),v(Y)) \\to \\Mor(u(v(X)), u(v(Y)))\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$v$", "MATH_0007": "$u$", "MATH_0008": "$v$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\Mor(v(X), v(Y)) \\to \\Mor(u(v(X)), u(v(Y))) \\to \\Mor(u(v(X)), Y)\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$u(v(Y)) \\to 